SUMMARY:Cross Currents: Improvised Truths — Curtis Patterson and the Jazz
  of Form
LOCATION:Hilliard Art Museum\, 710 E St Mary Blvd\, Lafayette
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Improvised Truths: Curtis Patterson and the Jazz of
  Form \, the latest iteration of Cross Currents\, a series using visual ar
 t as a catalyst for interdisciplinary dialogue\, as we explore how Patters
 on’s bronze and steel sculptures channel the improvisational language of
  jazz and African diasporic symbolism into visual metaphors of movement\, 
 continuity\, and cross-cultural memory.\n\n5:00 p.m. Doors Open\n\n5:30 p.
 m. Panel Discussion\n\n6:30 p.m. Jazz Performance\n\nRSVP HERE\n\nPanelist
 s\n\nDr. Sharlene Sinegal-DeCuir \, Professor of History and Chair of Afri
 can American and African Diaspora Studies\, Xavier University of Louisiana
 \n\nDonald Harrison Jr. \, saxophonist\, composer\, and Big Chief of the C
 ongo Square Nation Afro-New Orleans Cultural Group\n\nDr. Allison Young \,
  Associate Professor of Contemporary Art History\, LSU\n\nModerated by Dr.
  Joel Rhone \, Assistant Professor of Literature\, University of Louisiana
  Lafayette\n\nFree for museum members\, UL students\, faculty and staff. G
 eneral public entry with museum admission.\n\nPresented by Louisiana Endow
 ment for the Humanities\n\nFunding for the 2026 Rebirth Grant has been pro
 vided by the State of Louisiana and administered by the Louisiana Endowmen
 t for the Humanities.\n\nThe views\, findings\, conclusions\, or recommend
 ations expressed by this organization do not necessarily represent those o
 f either the Louisiana Endowment for the Humanities or the State of Louisi
 ana.\n\nhttps://hilliardartmuseum.org/event/cross-currents-improvised-trut
 hs-curtis-patterson-and-the-jazz-of-form/
